          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity 255a",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity 255a\n\nsanity test_255a spends nearly all of its time in\nladvise_willread_performance(), which does 10 iterations of\nthree passes that each do 25600 random 4KiB reads of a 100MB\nfile.  Those 30 passes of synchronous reads, each capped at\n60 seconds, take 1000-2000 seconds in CI.\n\nDo an eighth as many reads per pass and run 3 iterations\ninstead of 10.  The file stays 100MB, so the cold OSS cache\nversus willread comparison is unchanged; only the number of\nsamples averaged shrinks.\n\nThe willread threshold compared the willread speedup in\npercent with half the cached read rate in MB/s, a mixup\nreintroduced by LU-17527.  Fewer reads lower the absolute\nrate, which would move that threshold, so compare with half\nthe cached read speedup instead, as originally intended.\n\nOn a test VM cluster, ONLY=255a took 1089s and 2017s before\nand 170s, 166s, 137s and 252s after (the spread is VM disk\nspeed; the slow runs hit the 60s per pass cap).\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=255a\nFixes: e763a32e17f7 (\"LU-17527 tests: fix sanity/255a decimal comparison\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ic0da67345f16f477b493cc7dd16ee3b1cd42272a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
